    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d102">

                <pb facs="0207" n="137" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg137"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Edward M. House Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >House</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-19">November 19,
                            1918</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>18. I am delighted to receive your number 16.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d102-f1"/> I
                    am confident that everything will now work out satisfactorily. You will probably
                    be made Honorary President of the Congress and the French Prime Minister Acting
                    President.</p>
                <p>I am arranging with Pershing to have our army engineers make an approximate
                    estimate of the damage done in Belgium and France.<anchor n="15"
                        xml:id="d102-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d102-f1" n="14" xml:id="d102-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d102-f2" n="15" xml:id="d102-f2-content">
                <p>For additional correspondence on this subject, see <ref
                        target="frus1919Parisv02#pg_575">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>,
                        pp. 575</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
